# Agent and skill definitions are parsed by the harness; CRLF in frontmatter
# has broken registration before. Keep them LF regardless of platform.
*.md text eol=lf

# The `*.md` pin above was not enough on its own. The definition files three
# harnesses actually read are not Markdown: `.codex/agents/*.toml`,
# `.copilot/agents/*.json`, and the `exploration-charter` schema template.
# All were CRLF in the working tree with an empty `attr/`, because no pattern
# here claimed them. Same blast radius as the `.md` case, same fix.
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

# These pins govern what git writes on checkout and what it stores on commit.
# They do NOT reach the converters, which write to disk outside git entirely;
# that half is the newline="\n" argument in each convert-agents.py. Extension
# patterns also cannot cover an extensionless definition such as `kflow`.
# sdlc-suite/tools/eol_check.py is the byte-level check that covers both gaps,
# including untracked definitions git cannot see.
